==================================================================================
SUMMAND (antidiagonals, +) vs MULTIPLICAND (hyperbolas, x) -- geometry & LRC
==================================================================================

(0) IN-DEGREE GEOMETRY (incoming-pair counts; the two foliations):
   n : summand floor((n-1)/2) | multiplicand divisor-pairs (1..n)
    4 :   1                  |   1   
    6 :   2                  |   2   
    7 :   3                  |   1   (prime: only (1,p))
   12 :   5                  |   3   
   13 :   6                  |   1   (prime: only (1,p))
   14 :   6                  |   2   
   16 :   7                  |   2   
   24 :  11                  |   4   
   30 :  14                  |   4   
   36 :  17                  |   4   
   -> summand in-degree grows linearly (dense, additive); multiplicand stays tiny
      except at highly-composite n (sparse, multiplicative). Log map sends the
      hyperbola xy=n to the antidiagonal log x+log y=log n: multiplicand = summand
      in log-coordinates.

